ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON THE DEVELOPMENT OF THE FLORICULTURE INDUSTRY AND PROMOTION OF FLORAL CULTURE

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on the Development of the Floriculture Industry and Promotion of Floral Culture and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of Flowers and Ornamental Plants)
The term "those prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act on the Development of the Floriculture Industry and Promotion of Floral Culture (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means any of the following:
1. Cut flowers: Plants cultivated for use by cutting their flowers, stems, leaves, or other parts;
2. Orchids: Plants of the orchid family cultivated for ornamental purposes;
3. Foliage plants: Plants cultivated for ornamental appreciation of the shape, color, patterns, or other features of their leaves, excluding orchids;
4. Herbaceous flowering plants: Flowering herbaceous plants cultivated for use by planting them in flower beds or pots;
5. Flowering trees and shrubs: Flowering woody plants cultivated for landscaping or for ornamental purposes by planting them in pots;
6. Ornamental trees: Trees cultivated for landscaping to appreciate their foliage and tree form;
7. Bulbous plants: Plants cultivated for the use of their propagation bulbs, meaning the underground stems or roots of crops propagated by bulbs;
8. Seed plants: Plants cultivated for the use of their seeds;
9. Other plants determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 3 (Formulation and Implementation of Comprehensive Plans for the Development of the Floriculture Industry)
When the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs formulates or amends a comprehensive plan for the development of the floriculture industry under Article 5 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "comprehensive plan"), the Minister shall post its contents on the website of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 4 (Formulation and Implementation of Implementation Plans)
(1) When the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, or a Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as a "Mayor/Do Governor") formulates an implementation plan for the development of the floriculture industry and promotion of floral culture under Article 6 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "implementation plan"), the Mayor/Do Governor shall inform the heads of Si/Gun/Gu (the head of a Gu means the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) of its contents.
(2) A Mayor/Do Governor shall submit the performance results for the relevant year under the implementation plan to the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs by March 31 of the following year pursuant to Article 6 (3) of the Act.

Article 5 (Compilation of Statistics and Fact-Finding Surveys)
(1) The scope of the compilation of statistics and fact-finding surveys concerning the floriculture industry under Article 7(1) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. The status of cultivation of flowers and ornamental plants;
2. Surveys on the business operations of farms growing flowers and ornamental plants;
3. The status of distribution, sale, and consumption of flowers and ornamental plants;
4. The status of personnel engaged in the floriculture industry;
5. The status of imports and exports of flowers and ornamental plants by item and country;
6. Other matters necessary for the formulation and implementation of policies to develop the floriculture industry and promote floral culture.
(2) Fact-finding surveys under Article 7(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "fact-finding surveys") shall be conducted according to the following categories:
1. Regular surveys: To be conducted every five years, in the year immediately preceding the formulation of a comprehensive plan; provided that fact-finding surveys concerning paragraph (1) 1 and 5 shall be conducted annually;
2. Ad hoc surveys: To be conducted where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs deems them necessary for the formulation and implementation of policies to develop the floriculture industry and promote floral culture.
(3) Where necessary to conduct fact-finding surveys efficiently, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs may commission a research institution, corporation, or organization with expertise in the floriculture industry to conduct the surveys.
(4) The comprehensive information management system for flowers and ornamental plants under Article 7(3) of the Act shall include the following information:
1. The contents of fact-finding surveys;
2. The status of trading in flowers and ornamental plants at wholesale markets and joint markets established pursuant to Articles 17 and 43 of the Act on Distribution and Price Stabilization of Agricultural and Fishery Products;
3. Other matters necessary for the systematic management of information on the current state of the floriculture industry.
(5) The term "specialized institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7(4) of the Act means the Korea Agro-Fisheries and Food Trade Corporation under the Korea Agro-Fisheries and Food Trade Corporation Act.

Article 6 (Requirements and Procedures for Designating Floriculture Industry Promotion Areas)
(1) The Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs may, pursuant to Article 9(1) of the Act, designate an area that meets all of the following requirements as a floriculture industry promotion area (hereinafter referred to as a "promotion area"):
1. The area under cultivation of flowers and ornamental plants shall be at least 100,000 square meters, and the combined area under cultivation of flowers and ornamental plants and occupied by other floriculture industry facilities shall be at least 300,000 square meters;
2. The designation shall have the effect of promoting and developing the floriculture industry;
3. The project plan and financing plan for developing the promotion area shall be feasible and appropriate.
(2) A Mayor/Do Governor who intends to have an area designated as a promotion area under Article 9(1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs an application for designation, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, accompanied by a floriculture industry promotion plan that includes the following:
1. The name of the promotion area;
2. The location and area of the proposed area;
3. The current status of farming households cultivating flowers and ornamental plants, areas under cultivation, and other floriculture industry facilities within the proposed area;
4. The project plan and financing plan for developing the promotion area.
(3) Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs designates an area as a promotion area or cancels the designation of a promotion area under Article 9(1) or (3) of the Act, the Minister shall notify the relevant Mayor/Do Governor of that fact and post it on the website of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 7 (Requirements for Designating Specialized Agencies for the Promotion of Floral Culture, Etc.)
(1) The requirements for designating a specialized agency for the promotion of floral culture under Article 11(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "specialized agency") shall be as set forth in Attached Table 1.
(2) A person who intends to obtain designation as a specialized agency under Article 11(1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs an application for designation, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, accompanied by documents proving that the requirements for designation under paragraph (1) are met.
(3) A specialized agency shall perform the following functions:
1. Support for incorporating flowers and ornamental plants into daily life and promoting their use;
2. Support for the dissemination of horticultural therapy programs using flowers and ornamental plants;
3. Support for the dissemination of educational programs using flowers and ornamental plants;
4. Establishment of a system for cooperation with persons engaged in the floriculture industry, relevant institutions and organizations, and others;
5. Other functions necessary to promote floral culture.
(4) The detailed criteria for dispositions revoking the designation of a specialized agency or suspending its operations under Article 11(3) of the Act shall be as set forth in Attached Table 2.
(5) Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs designates a specialized agency, revokes its designation, or orders the suspension of its operations under Article 11(1) or (3) of the Act, the Minister shall post that fact on the website of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 8 (Labeling Information and Methods for Reused Flower Wreaths)
(1) The information to be indicated on wreaths made using reused fresh flowers under Article 14(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "reused flower wreaths") shall be as follows:
1. The indication "reused flower wreaths";
2. The seller's trade name (in the case of a person who produces, stores, or displays the wreaths, meaning the trade name of the person who produces, stores, or displays them) and telephone number.
(2) The labeling information for reused flower wreaths under paragraph (1) shall be indicated on the front of the wreaths in a manner readily recognizable to consumers, and specific labeling methods, including the position and size of the labeling, shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.
(3) Where a person selling reused flower wreaths sells such wreaths in a cybermall under subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the Act on the Consumer Protection in Electronic Commerce, Etc., the person shall provide the labeling for reused flower wreaths on the front of the wreaths in accordance with paragraphs (1) and (2), and shall indicate on that cybermall that they are "reused flower wreaths", as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 9 (Inspections of Labeling of Reused Flower Wreaths)
(1) Inspections under Article 16(1) of the Act to ascertain whether reused flower wreaths are labeled, whether the labeling information and methods, etc. are appropriate, and whether there are any violations shall be conducted as periodic inspections and ad hoc inspections. Periodic inspections shall be conducted at least once a year, and ad hoc inspections shall be conducted whenever deemed necessary.
(2) Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or a Mayor/Do Governor intends to conduct an inspection under paragraph (1), the Minister or Mayor/Do Governor shall formulate an inspection plan that includes the purpose, period, subjects, and methods, etc. of the inspection.
(3) Relevant public officials conducting inspections pursuant to Article 16(1) of the Act shall carry identification prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs and present it to the persons concerned.

Article 10 (Delegation of Authority)
The Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs shall delegate the following authority to the head of the National Agricultural Products Quality Management Service pursuant to Article 18(1) of the Act:
1. Inspections of labeling of reused flower wreaths under Article 16(1) of the Act;
2. Management of honorary monitors and payment of expenses under Article 16(2) of the Act;
3. Imposition and collection of administrative fines under Article 21(1) of the Act.

Article 11 (Standards for Imposing Administrative Fines)
